      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This order is twice that limit. It would raise the risk of serious GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nIf you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. Include the clinical rationale, and I'll enter it with a note on the order."
      }
